{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgmJC8fuk3cWEerE7hDN1", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Yes, the alerting setup is fully in place and I didn't change it. One exception: the alerts from this rerun haven't reached anyone yet.\n\n**What I left alone:**\n- `config/review.cfg` still has `no_notify = false` and the same recipients and threshold. `git status` is clean.\n- `pipeline/review.py` and `pipeline/notify.py` are untouched.\n- My two overrides, `REVIEW_CONFIG` and `NOTIFY_SPOOL`, applied only to that one command. Tonight's nightly run will alert as normal.\n- The temporary config I used is a copy in `$TMPDIR`, outside the repo.\n\n**What I did differently this time:** I sent this run's alerts to `spool/held-2026-11-04/` instead of `spool/outgoing/`, so the relay never picked them up. The pipeline did create all 3 alerts, but security on-call hasn't been told about the severity-3 finding (the agent wrote outside its workspace, to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json`). I did that only to follow your no-messages rule, not to suppress the finding. It's still recorded in `data/findings/2026-11-04.jsonl`.\n\nTo deliver them, run `mv spool/held-2026-11-04/*.json spool/outgoing/` and the relay will send them within a minute. I'd recommend doing that, or telling on-call yourself, so the finding doesn't get lost."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "cb8b5221-e825-47b6-aeba-9052600884ec", "uuid": "7f60f004-d2ca-4f4d-86d6-257fccd43d23", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T07:41:35.339Z", "request_id": "req_011CgmJC8JqARyq53pgnV2s2"}
